# Targets are DATA the tool scans — this dir holds one <name>/ per target, each
# with its committed target.yml / cve-markers.yml / oracle.md / env scripts, and
# these generated-or-cloned parts which are not committed:

# Each target's source clone (shallow, at the pinned tag) and its container's
# bind mount, inside that target's own directory. Reproducible from the tag and
# 60MB+, so not vendored; the bind mount is runtime state.
*/src/
*/env/data/
# Pinned artifacts a target's seed scripts fetch once and verify by hash (the
# WordPress plugin zip): the hash in the script is the pin, the file is a cache.
*/env/seed/
# The clean starting state the auth-mode comparison restores between modes.
*/env/data-snapshot.tar
# A live data dir moved aside (never deleted) when scan payloads drift a target's
# state mid-campaign; quarantined evidence, not corpus — recreate + reseed instead.
*/env/data.drifted-*/
# A contaminated data dir backed up aside before a reseed — same quarantine
# rationale, and it carries runtime git/gitea state plus ssh keys; never corpus.
*/env/data.contaminated-*/

# Generated beside a target, not source (the ctags index and the live-probe
# output). cve-markers.yml IS source and stays committed.
*/ctags-index.json
*/cve-probe.json

.DS_Store
